# SourceDesk example configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` if you want to keep credentials in your shell
# environment while developing. Note that this is a *development convenience only*:
#
#   - The shipped application NEVER reads a .env file. API keys are entered in
#     Settings → AI Providers and stored in the macOS Keychain.
#   - A `.env` file is git-ignored. Never commit real keys, and never paste a key
#     into a source file, a test fixture or an issue.
#
# Everything below is optional. SourceDesk runs fully locally, with no keys at all,
# using a local model and a keyless search provider.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local models (recommended default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the local model server listens. Ollama's default is shown.
SOURCEDESK_OLLAMA_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# A model to pull for local answers. See README → "Setting up a local model".
# SOURCEDESK_OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.2

# An embedding model, if you want semantic search better than the built-in
# lexical embedder. Leave unset to use the built-in (zero-download) embedder.
# SOURCEDESK_OLLAMA_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud providers (optional; billed by the vendor, and separate from any
# consumer subscription — a ChatGPT Plus or Claude Pro plan is not an API key)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# OpenAI, or any gateway implementing POST /v1/chat/completions.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# SOURCEDESK_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Anthropic Messages API, or a compliant gateway in front of it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# SOURCEDESK_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web search (optional). DuckDuckGo needs no key and is the default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Brave Search API — independent index, free tier available.
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=...

# Tavily — returns extracted page content with each result.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=...

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Development and testing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Run the test suites that touch the public internet (off by default, because
# tests should not depend on someone else's server being up).
# SOURCEDESK_LIVE_WEB=1

# Use a scratch library instead of the real one, for tests and screenshots.
# SOURCEDESK_SEED_ROOT=/tmp/sd-demo/Library/Application Support/SourceDesk
# SOURCEDESK_SCREENSHOT_ROOT=/tmp/sd-shots
